      "explanation": "These five words are the building blocks of polite conversation in Hindi. Using 'kripaya' and 'shukriya' frequently will make a great impression."
    },
    {
      "id": "hi-s1-l3-ex02",
      "type": "multiple_choice",
      "question": "How do you say 'please' in Hindi?",
      "options": [
        "kripaya",
        "shukriya",
        "maaf kijiye",
        "dhanyavaad"
      ],
      "correctIndex": 0,
      "explanation": "'Kripaya' means 'please'. It is used to make requests polite, just like in English. For example: 'kripaya baithiye' (please sit down)."
    },
    {
      "id": "hi-s1-l3-ex03",
      "type": "translation",
      "prompt": "How do you say 'excuse me' or 'sorry' formally in Hindi?",
      "direction": "from_english",
      "correct": "maaf kijiye",
      "acceptedVariants": [
        "maaf kiijiye"
      ],
      "explanation": "'Maaf kijiye' is the formal way to say sorry or excuse me. 'Maaf' means forgiveness and 'kijiye' is a polite request form.",
      "hint": "sounds like: maaf kijiye"
    },
    {
      "id": "hi-s1-l3-ex04",
